program over_indent_warning

? An over-indented statement after a closed block still belongs to the
? enclosing block (only `$` closes it); the compiler warns about the
? indent instead of failing with "Unexpected token indent". The guarded
? line below runs in the main body (not inside the if), so x becomes 15.

@ main ||:
	expected: []
	expected.push|"15"|

	x: 5
	if x is 99 then
		x = 99
	$
		x = x + 10
	print|x|
	print|expected|
$
